# Hustronix product stack

## Architecture

- **Backend**: Node + Express + WebSocket in [`apps/api/src/server.ts`](../../apps/api/src/server.ts), SQLite via [`apps/api/src/database.ts`](../../apps/api/src/database.ts). Default HTTP port **3005** (`PORT`).
- **Frontend**: Next.js App Router in [`apps/web/`](../../apps/web/). Default dev port **3000**. Production = unified process (API + WS + Next) unless deliberately split behind a reverse proxy.

## Environment

**API (root `.env`):** `PORT`, `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` (comma-separated; must include the Next origin, e.g. `http://localhost:3000`), `MISSION_CONTROL_API_KEY`, LLM keys as needed.

**Anthropic routing (server):** Coordinator uses **premium** tier (`ANTHROPIC_MODEL_PREMIUM` or legacy `ANTHROPIC_MODEL`; default **`claude-sonnet-4-6`**). Sub-agents / intelligence use **fast** tier (`ANTHROPIC_MODEL_FAST`; default **`claude-haiku-4-5-20251001`**). Optional **`LLM_COORDINATOR_HAIKU=1`** forces the main coordinator onto the fast Haiku model (much cheaper). Retired snapshot ids redirect at runtime; fast tier rejects non-Haiku ids. SQLite `anthropicModel` overrides premium when env omits premium/legacy model. **`GET /api/health`** returns `llmConfigured`, `anthropicPremiumModel`, and `anthropicFastModel` (no secrets). **Cost-saver mode is default** (tighter history/iterations/caps); disable with `LLM_COST_SAVER=0`. OpenAI default chat model is **`gpt-4o-mini`** (`OPENAI_CHAT_MODEL`).

**UI (`apps/web/.env.local`):**

- **`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`** — Absolute API origin (e.g. `http://127.0.0.1:3005`) **or leave unset / empty** so browser calls same-origin `/api/*` (recommended with cookies).
- **`API_PROXY_TARGET`** (server-only, Next rewrites) — Where Next proxies `/api/:path*` when using same-origin mode; default `http://127.0.0.1:3005`.
- **`NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL`** — Chat WebSocket (e.g. `ws://127.0.0.1:3005`). On localhost, [`api.ts`](../../apps/web/src/lib/api.ts) can fall back to port 3005 when HTTP base is empty.
- Optional **`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_KEY`** + stored **`hustronix_userId`** (automation only; sent as **`x-api-key` + `x-user-id`**). Normal UI auth uses the session cookie only.

## Auth contract

- REST [`authMiddleware`](../../apps/api/src/middleware/auth.ts): **`Bearer hx_live_…`** → cookie **`hustronix_session`** → optional legacy **`hustronix_uid`** (`ALLOW_LEGACY_UID_COOKIE=1`) → **`x-api-key` + `x-user-id`** (user must exist). No ambient **`system`** on loopback; use **`ALLOW_LOOPBACK_AUTH=1`** + API key for local scripts.
- RBAC via [`authorization.ts`](../../apps/api/src/security/authorization.ts): role from **`org.owner_user_id`** / **`org.role`** (default **viewer**); mutators use **`requirePermission`**.
- Passwords: **bcrypt** (12 rounds); legacy SHA-256 verifies once then upgrades. Rate limits on **`/api/auth/register`**, **`/api/auth/login`**, **`/api/auth/password`** ([`rateLimit.ts`](../../apps/api/src/middleware/rateLimit.ts)).
- **`POST /api/auth/logout`** revokes the session matching the cookie. Sessions + API keys: **`GET/POST/DELETE /api/auth/api-keys`**, **`GET/DELETE /api/auth/sessions`**, **`POST /api/auth/sessions/revoke-all`**. Profile updates: **`PATCH /api/me`** → `settings` keys **`profile.*`** (writable keys allowlisted in [`settings-keys.ts`](../../apps/api/src/security/settings-keys.ts)).
- **`external_signals.user_id`** scopes per-tenant signals; **`system`** automation principal does not receive cross-tenant signal reads.
- WebSocket: session cookie; optional **`?session=`** when **`ALLOW_WS_SESSION_QUERY=1`**; loopback **`?userId=`** only with **`ALLOW_LOOPBACK_AUTH=1`** + API key ([`resolveWsAuth`](../../apps/api/src/middleware/auth.ts)).
- UI **`credentials: "include"`** ([`api.ts`](../../apps/web/src/lib/api.ts)); **`hustronix_userId`** in localStorage is optional dev automation pairing with **`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_KEY`** only.

**Proxy note:** Same-origin `/api` rewrites help cookies; if `Set-Cookie` is dropped by a proxy, align cookie `Domain`/`Path` or terminate auth at the edge.

## Wired UI routes (live API)

| Route | Behavior |
|-------|----------|
| `/mission-control` | `GET /api/mission-control/summary`, `GET /api/decisions`, `POST /api/decisions/commit`, WebSocket `COMMIT_DECISION` |
| `/execute` | `GET /api/execution/ledger?scope=all`, `GET /api/execution/capacity`, `POST /api/execution/transition` |
| `/signals` | `GET /api/execution/signals/by-state`, `POST /api/execution/link` |
| `/chat` | WebSocket: `text`, `text_chunk`, `history`, `new_session` |
| `/reports` | `GET /api/metrics/reports` |
| `/teams` | `GET /api/metrics/teams` |
| `/profile` | `GET/PATCH /api/me`, `GET /api/activity`, `GET/POST/DELETE /api/auth/api-keys`, sessions endpoints |
| `/settings` | `GET /api/settings`, `POST /api/settings/bulk` (General + Notifications toggles mapped to `PREF.*`) |

## Public marketing API

| Endpoint | Behavior |
|----|----|
| `POST /api/early-access` | Early access waitlist (SQLite `early_access_leads`, optional SMTP notify via `EARLY_ACCESS_TO` / `CONTACT_TO`) |

## Marketing surfaces

- **Product landing** (`/`, Next) — Sign in / Get Started → `/login`, `/signup`; hero and pricing CTAs point at the app.
- **Demand-validation static site** (`netlify-landing/`) — early-access + contact forms only; no product app links. Regenerate with `node scripts/export-netlify-landing.mjs` (sanitizes after export). API: **`POST /api/early-access`**, **`POST /api/contact`** (SQLite + optional SMTP).

